# Catalog Arabic naming — brand as-is

`nameAr` always starts with the brand exactly as written on the pack, then a dash, then Iraqi-market Arabic product copy.

- If the brand is English/Latin (`ARTDECO`, `GOSH`, `Seventeen`, `Maybelline`) keep it English at the start of `nameAr`. Do **not** translate it to Arabic in the title.
- If the brand is Arabic (`حياة`) keep it Arabic.
- `brand_ar` on the brand record may still have an Arabic alias; that alias is **not** the `nameAr` prefix when `brand_en` is Latin.

Format:

```
nameAr: "{BrandAsIs} - {نوع سوقي} {خط EN} {صفة} {حجم}"
nameEn: "{BrandEn} - {Official Product Name}"
```

Examples:

- `Seventeen - كونسيلر Ideal Cover Liquid بتغطية كاملة`
- `ARTDECO - جلوس شفاه Plumping Lip Fluid مملّئ 3 مل`
- `ARTDECO - موس تنظيف Pure Silk 150 مل`
- `حياة - سيروم فيتامين سي للوجه 30 مل`

Phone add (`admin-mobile`) must auto-prefix titles when brand is chosen or on next/save. AI autofill (`polishNaming`) must use `brandPrefixForArabicTitle`.
